      "side": 1,
      "message": "The following excerpts from the commit message are useful information:\n\n\u003e A block can only copy from its own tile.\n\n\u003e Give each tile its own table with only the blocks that lie inside it.\n\u003e The encoder threads build the tables before the tiles are encoded, one\n\u003e tile per job, and av1_intrabc_hash_search() uses the table of the\n\u003e current tile. A frame with more than 16 tiles keeps a single\n\u003e table for the whole frame, which bounds the memory.\n\n\u003e The bucket arrays are now allocated only for the block sizes that get\n\u003e built. At speed 11 that is just 8x8.\n\nPlease make sure that this information also appears in some comments in the source code.",
      "revId": "28400443440ae9fdc578323a93bd951f629fa5de",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
